{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review Equality Act and include physical appearance, with guidance and examples",
        "additional_details": "\u200bWe are concerned by the risks of systemic appearance-based discrimination (\"lookism\") harming individuals in employment and healthcare. In workplaces, people can face superficial judgments. In healthcare, we are concerned that chronic patients are routinely dismissed because of visual judgments like \"looking well.\" I urge the Government to establish legal protections.",
        "background": "I ask the Government to review the Equality Act and add legal protections for physical appearance, stating what may constitute discrimination on this basis at work or in healthcare such as decisions taken about people influenced by physical looks and features, appearance of health or clothing.",
